'''The 2009–10 season''' was the 116th season of competitive [[2009–10 in Scottish football|football]] by [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]].

Celtic started their 2009–10 campaign by playing in the pre-season [[Wembley Cup]]. Their first competitive game of the season was at [[Celtic Park]] on 29 July where they were beaten 1–0 by [[FC Dynamo Moscow|Dynamo Moscow]] in the 1st leg of the [[2009–10 UEFA Champions League|Champions League]] [[2009–10 UEFA Champions League qualifying phase and play-off round#Third qualifying round|third-qualifying round]] for best placed teams. However, in the return leg at [[Dynamo Stadium (Moscow)|Dynamo Stadium]] on 5 August, Celtic won 2–0 (2–1 on aggregate) thanks to a 44th-minute goal by [[Scott McDonald]] and a late injury-time strike from [[Georgios Samaras]], giving Celtic a first away win in Europe since their 1–0 win over [[MTK Hungária FC|MTK Hungaria]] at [[Stadium Puskás Ferenc]] in 2003. The win took Celtic through to the Champions League play-off round, where they lost to [[Arsenal F.C.|Arsenal]].

Celtic kicked off their [[2009–10 Scottish Premier League|Scottish Premier League]] campaign with a 3–1 win over [[Aberdeen F.C.|Aberdeen]] at [[Pittodrie Stadium]]. After 30 games of the season, [[Tony Mowbray]] was sacked following Celtic's 4–0 loss to [[St Mirren F.C.|St Mirren]], with Celtic 10 points behind league leaders Rangers. [[Neil Lennon]] was then appointed [[caretaker manager]] until the end of the season; his first match in charge was a 3–1 victory over [[Kilmarnock F.C.|Kilmarnock]] on 27 March. Lennon won all the remaining league games, but was unable to prevent Rangers from winning the league title.

Celtic lost their [[Scottish Cup]] semi-final against [[Ross County F.C.|Ross County]] 2–0. This was Lennon's only defeat during his tenure as interim manager.<ref>[http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport1/hi/football/teams/c/celtic/8668281.stm Neil Lennon pleased with Celtic record] BBC Sport, 7 May 2010</ref> After the end of the season, Lennon succeeded Tony Mowbray as the next Celtic manager on a permanent basis.

